<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0c0c0c">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

    {%- comment -%}
      Favicon. No longer blocked: the NON Somm mark supplies the square icon the
      brand never had. The wordmark on the CDN is 3000x1072 and a 2.8:1 logotype
      squeezed into 32x32 is an illegible smear, which is why nothing was set.

      Sizes rather than one 32px PNG: 32 is the tab, 180 is the iOS home screen,
      and Safari asks for the apple-touch-icon by name whether or not you supply
      one — without it, iOS crops a screenshot of the page instead.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="192x192" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 192, height: 192 }}">
      <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The NON Somm mark, shipped as a theme asset rather than waiting on a
        Files upload. It is the full stop from "NON." held in its typographic
        position — baseline, left, never centred; the offset is the mark. Sharp
        corners deliberately: NON has no soft corners anywhere.

        SVG scales to every slot from the 16px tab up, so there is no PNG set to
        keep in sync. Safari asks for apple-touch-icon by name and will not take
        an SVG for it, so that one line is intentionally absent rather than
        pointing at a file that would not render — iOS falls back to a page
        screenshot, which is the lesser of the two wrong answers.

        Setting a favicon in Theme settings still wins; this is the floor.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ 'non-somm-favicon.svg' | asset_url }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    <title>
      {{ page_title }}
      {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: current_tags | join: ', ' }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif -%}
      {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
    </title>

    {%- if page_description -%}
      <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
    {%- elsif settings.meta_description != blank -%}
      <meta name="description" content="{{ settings.meta_description | escape }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {% render 'meta-tags' %}
    {% render 'structured-data' %}

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    {%- comment -%}
      Two faces only: Helvetica Neue (self-hosted, see theme.css) and JetBrains
      Mono for everything that is not Helvetica.

      Newsreader used to be loaded here. It is a serif, which the brand does not
      use, and it was referenced by exactly nothing in the theme — a
      render-blocking request for a font that could not have rendered. It came
      across with the design export.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet">

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'theme.css' | asset_url }}">
    {%- comment -%}
      Motion. Loaded once for the whole document rather than per section,
      because a single IntersectionObserver watching every band is cheaper
      than one per section and the stagger has to reason across siblings.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script src="{{ 'reveal.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    <script>
      window.NON = {
        routes: {
          cart_add: '{{ routes.cart_add_url }}.js',
          cart_change: '{{ routes.cart_change_url }}.js',
          cart_update: '{{ routes.cart_update_url }}.js',
          cart: '{{ routes.cart_url }}.js',
          cart_page: '{{ routes.cart_url }}',
          predictive_search: '{{ routes.predictive_search_url }}'
        },
        settings: {
          cartDrawer: {{ settings.cart_drawer | default: true | json }},
          freeShipping: {% render 'free-shipping', mode: 'json' %},
          moneyFormat: {{ shop.money_format | json }},
          sommEndpoint: {{ settings.somm_endpoint | default: '' | json }},
          sommStream: {{ settings.somm_stream | default: true | json }},
          sommTypeSpeed: {{ settings.somm_type_speed | default: 12 | json }},
          lottoEndpoint: {{ settings.lotto_endpoint | default: '' | json }}
        },
        strings: {
          sommError: {{ 'sections.somm.error' | t | json }},
          lottoUnavailable: {{ 'sections.lotto.unavailable' | t | json }},
          cartEmpty: {{ 'cart.general.empty' | t | json }},
          soldOut: {{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t | json }},
          freeShippingProgress: {{ 'cart.general.free_shipping_progress' | t: amount: '[amount]' | json }},
          freeShippingMet: {{ 'cart.general.free_shipping_met' | t | json }},
          {%- comment -%}
            Ask-a-human. Every one of these is a locale key rather than a
            literal in somm.js, which has no access to the locale files — the
            same reason the lotto's done-label is passed in from Liquid.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          askHead: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_head' | t | json }},
          askWhy: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_why' | t | json }},
          askBodyLabel: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_body_label' | t | json }},
          askEmail: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_email' | t | json }},
          askSend: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_send' | t | json }},
          askSending: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_sending' | t | json }},
          askNeedEmail: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_need_email' | t | json }},
          askNeedBody: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_need_body' | t | json }},
          askSent: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_sent' | t | json }},
          askFailed: {{ 'sections.somm.ask_failed' | t | json }},
          {%- comment -%}
            The mobile sheet's own copy. Same reason as the block above: the
            recommendation card is built in JavaScript, which cannot reach the
            locale files, so every word it prints is handed to it from here.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          sommSlow: {{ 'sections.somm.slow' | t | json }},
          sommFailHead: {{ 'sections.somm.fail_head' | t | json }},
          sommFailBody: {{ 'sections.somm.fail_body' | t | json }},
          sommRetry: {{ 'sections.somm.retry' | t | json }},
          sommShopRange: {{ 'sections.somm.shop_range' | t | json }},
          sommRecAdd: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_add' | t | json }},
          sommRecAdding: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_adding' | t | json }},
          sommRecAdded: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_added' | t | json }},
          sommRecAddFailed: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_add_failed' | t | json }},
          sommRecSee: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_see' | t | json }},
          sommRecWhy: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_why' | t | json }},
          sommRecAnother: {{ 'sections.somm.rec_another' | t | json }}
        }
      };
    </script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Feature events, loaded before anything that reports them.

      Standard analytics measures whether people ARRIVED. This measures whether
      the thing they touched WORKED — which is the gap the dead pairing chips
      lived in for weeks while every metric looked normal.

      Deliberately first: somm.js, pairing.js and collection.js all guard with
      `if (window.NON && NON.track)`, so they degrade to silence rather than
      throwing if this ever fails to load. Nothing depends on it to function.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script src="{{ 'non-events.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    <script src="{{ 'cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    {{ content_for_header }}

    {%- comment -%}
      PRELOAD THE PRODUCT'S FIRST IMAGE.

      It is the largest thing on a product page and the thing a customer is
      waiting for, but the browser cannot find it until it has parsed the
      section that renders it. Announcing it in the head starts the download
      with the stylesheet rather than after it.

      imagesrcset and imagesizes mirror the img exactly. If they drift, the
      browser downloads one file for the preload and a different one for the
      tag, which is slower than not preloading at all — so the sizes string
      here and the one in main-product.liquid are the same string, and any
      change to one has to be made to both.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if template.name == 'product' and product.featured_media -%}
      <link
        rel="preload"
        as="image"
        fetchpriority="high"
        href="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 900, format: 'webp' }}"
        imagesrcset="{{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 400, format: 'webp' }} 400w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 600, format: 'webp' }} 600w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 900, format: 'webp' }} 900w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp' }} 1200w, {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 1400, format: 'webp' }} 1400w"
        imagesizes="(min-width: 860px) 46vw, 100vw">
    {%- endif -%}
  </head>

  <body class="template-{{ template.name | handle }}">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">{{ 'general.accessibility.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>

    <div class="non-shell">
      {% sections 'header-group' %}

      <main id="main" role="main">
        {{ content_for_layout }}
      </main>

      {% sections 'footer-group' %}
    </div>

    {% render 'cart-drawer' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      The mobile Somm sheet, on the templates that carry an entry point.

      Gated rather than global because the brief asks that Somm code load only
      where something can open it: the homepage hero and triptych, and the
      product page's contextual entry. On every other template the snippet and
      its script are simply absent — not hidden, absent.

      One sheet, after the cart drawer in source order so the drawer wins the
      stacking context if both are ever up. The sheet closes itself when the
      drawer opens, so that should not happen; this is the belt to that braces.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if template.name == 'index' or template.name == 'product' -%}
      {% render 'somm-sheet' %}
    {%- endif -%}

    {% section 'non-lotto' %}
  </body>
</html>
